# RTL / LTR & Responsive

The app runs **RTL by default** (`ar`) and **LTR** (`en`). Every screen,
component, and primitive must work correctly in both, at every breakpoint.

## 1. Logical Properties — Never Physical
Use CSS logical (direction-aware) Tailwind utilities. Physical left/right
utilities are a bug — they don't flip for `ar`.

| ❌ Physical | ✅ Logical |
|---|---|
| `ml-*` / `mr-*` | `ms-*` / `me-*` |
| `pl-*` / `pr-*` | `ps-*` / `pe-*` |
| `left-*` / `right-*` | `start-*` / `end-*` |
| `ml-auto` / `mr-auto` | `ms-auto` / `me-auto` |
| `border-l` / `border-r` | `border-s` / `border-e` |
| `rounded-l-*` / `rounded-r-*` | `rounded-s-*` / `rounded-e-*` |
| `text-left` / `text-right` | `text-start` / `text-end` |
| `inset-l-*` / `inset-r-*` | `inset-s-*` / `inset-e-*` (or `inset-x-*` if symmetric) |
| `float-left` / `float-right` | `float-start` / `float-end` |

**Allowed physical usage** (symmetric — same in both directions):
- Centering: `left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2`, `inset-x-0`, `mx-auto`.
- Radix/vaul-managed animation classes keyed on `data-[side=…]` /
  `data-[vaul-drawer-direction=…]` — the library sets `data-side` from the
  *actual* resolved placement, so `data-[side=left]:slide-in-from-right-2` is
  correct; leave these.
- `cursor-w-resize` / `cursor-e-resize` on resize handles.

## 2. Directional Icons
- Chevrons/arrows that imply direction (breadcrumb separator, "next/prev",
  accordion/submenu carets, back buttons, pagination arrows) must flip in RTL:
  `className="rtl:rotate-180"` (or `className="rtl:-scale-x-100"`).
- Icons with no direction meaning (check, X, search, trash, bell) never flip.
- Chevron-down for dropdowns/accordions does **not** flip (vertical).

## 3. Text & Content
- No text chosen by locale/direction — always `t()` keys (@i18n.md).
- `dir="auto"` on inputs/textareas that accept free user text of unknown language.
- Numbers, code, phone numbers stay LTR: wrap in `<bdi>` or `dir="ltr"` when
  inline with RTL text.

## 4. Mobile-First & Responsive
- Design mobile-first: base classes target small screens, add `sm: md: lg: xl:`
  upward. Don't write desktop styles then undo them at `max-*`.
- Every page usable from ~360px wide. No horizontal page scroll — wide content
  (tables, charts, code) scrolls inside its own `overflow-x-auto` container.
- Touch targets ≥ 40px (`h-10`/`size-10`) for anything tappable on mobile.
- Sidebar collapses to a sheet on mobile (shell handles it); the sheet opens from
  the **start** side (right in `ar`, left in `en`).
- Stat grids stack (`grid-cols-1`) then widen (`sm:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4`).
- Use `@/hooks/use-mobile` only when layout must genuinely differ; prefer CSS
  breakpoints.
- Test each view at 360 / 768 / 1280 in both `ar` and `en`.

## 5. `components/ui/*` Primitives
- All primitives in `components/ui/` are kept RTL-safe: logical utilities,
  flipping directional icons, no physical positioning of adornments (dropdown
  check marks, select carets, input affixes use `end-*`/`start-*`).
- When adding or upgrading a primitive (shadcn CLI), immediately convert any
  physical utilities it ships with to logical ones before committing.
- `components/ui/direction.tsx` (`DirectionProvider`) is wired at the root from
  the i18next locale — don't add another.

## 6. Audit Checklist (per component / page)
1. Render in `ar` — is anything on the wrong side (icons, padding, borders,
   absolute-positioned elements, menu indicators)?
2. Grep the file for `\b(ml-|mr-|pl-|pr-|left-|right-|text-left|text-right|border-l|border-r|rounded-l|rounded-r)\b` — each hit is either converted or justified as symmetric (§1).
3. Do directional icons flip? (§2)
4. Does it reflow cleanly at 360px? Any horizontal overflow?
5. Are all strings `t()` keys with `ar` + `en` entries?
